WEBVTT

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.830
Whoa, have you lost weight, Yamada-<i>san</i>?

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:21.710
Huh?

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.800
You totally have!
Your tummy's way flatter!

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.800
My diet must be working!

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.640
H-Hey, Watanabe-<i>san</i>?

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.600
Sugimoto-<i>san</i>, what's that
pose you're doing?

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.770
I-It's the Winter Troupe's special pose!
How do you not know that, Watanabe-<i>san</i>?!

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.190
Every Kouka fan knows that!

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.900
Watanabe-<i>san</i>, I've been meaning
to ask this for quite a while,

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.870
but do you like any <i>other </i>shows
besides <i>The Rose of Versailles</i>?

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:58.330
Umm, well, I don't know
many other shows...

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:01.370
Look! You've traumatized
our poor class rep!

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:05.090
Sugimoto-<i>san </i>loves
the Winter Troupe most of all!

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.670
Uh, Sugimoto-<i>san</i>?

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:09.550
This is fine.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.590
No, this is wonderful!

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:15.760
Oh, Watanabe-<i>san</i>, we're going to see a
Winter Troupe performance this afternoon.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.180
They're doing <i>Romeo and Juliet</i>.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:24.100
This is the perfect chance for you to
fall in love with a show that isn't <i>RoV</i>!

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.440
We get to see a show?!

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.980
Yes, a few shows every year!

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:32.610
Seeing shows is an important part
of our Kouka education!

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:08.120
The Chosen Maidens

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:10.840
It's just like the theater I went to
in Tokyo when I was little!

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:13.380
Shh! Quiet down, Watanabe-<i>san</i>!

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:14.590
Oh, right!

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.890
Um, Watanabe-<i>san</i>, I--

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:19.970
Hey, you're from JPX!

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:24.180
C'mon, don't point it out, Sei!

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.640
Oh, sorry.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.940
Good afternoon, ma'am!

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:33.030
You in the hundredth class?
You girls are so cute.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.900
How's the Phantom doing?

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.110
Andou-<i>sensei </i>is doing well, thank you!

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:39.320
He's an ex-actor,

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.950
so he's always had trouble
fitting in with the other teachers.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.950
Help make his life easier, okay?

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.080
Of course!

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.380
Who was that lovely lady?!

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:56.130
You don't know?! She's the number two star
in the Winter Troupe, Sei Satomi!

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.220
Sei-<i>sama </i>isn't in today's show.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.220
I wish we could've seen her Tybalt.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:05.270
Tybalt is double-cast in this show.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:07.430
Wait, this show is the final performance

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.350
of the Winter Troupe's
top star, Sou Kazahana.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:16.240
But if Sei-<i>sama </i>isn't going to be
taking over for the rest of the shows,

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:17.320
then that means...

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:21.450
Sei Satomi-<i>sama </i>might be
the next top star of the Winter Troupe!

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.160
Your nose is bleeding!

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.370
So that means I was just talking to
the next top star of the troupe?

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:31.000
That's right! We're <i>so </i>lucky today!

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:36.760
Hey, Taichi, what am I supposed to do?

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:41.840
I said something horrible to Watanabe-<i>san</i>.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:47.100
I want to apologize, but I've never
fought with a friend before.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.890
I don't know how to make up with someone!

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:56.860
You speak of peace between
the Capulets and Montagues? What folly!

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:00.650
There is naught 'twixt
our families but hate, villain!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.580
Romeo!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:16.800
O, Juliet! Let us be one in death!

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:24.970
Let hate return to hate,
and love return to love!

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:27.430
My love is forever yours, Romeo!

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.910
<i>This </i>is Kouka...

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.120
That was so wonderful!

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:57.000
We'll get to stand on that stage
in two years' time.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.340
I know! I'm so excited!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:04.180
O, how my heart races!

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:09.810
I would fly o'er these walls
with these wings of love for you!

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:12.430
Those are Romeo's lines.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:16.190
Watanabe-<i>san </i>hasn't seen
any other show besides <i>RoV</i>, right?

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:19.020
So she memorized them
after hearing them just once?

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:24.240
With what words should I profess
my deepest love for you?

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:26.280
O, Juliet!

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:29.120
Look! Upon the pitch-black
curtain of night...

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:32.830
...sparkle a thousand brilliant stars!

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.830
Everyone must have noticed it
in that moment.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:40.090
Without thinking, they looked up to
the sky and saw themselves there.

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:42.090
But did they see what I saw?

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:45.470
That amongst the sea of glimmering stars,
there was one bright star,

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:47.430
shining above all others?

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:58.060
Twinkling high in the sky,
brighter than any in its midst...

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.650
That star was Sarasa Watanabe.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:03.280
That was where she belonged.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.900
Where I belonged.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:08.160
I want to see the world from up there.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:17.250
Don't think too hard about
what you want her to think about you.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:19.840
Work up your courage
to express your feelings

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:24.260
and speak them, honest and true,
with words of love.

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:27.130
Um, I...

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:31.180
I want to be friends
with you, Watanabe-<i>san</i>!

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:36.850
I'm so glad!

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:45.320
I thought my feelings
would be one-sided forever.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:49.870
Ever since the first moment
I met you, Ai-<i>chan</i>,

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:52.870
I knew I wanted to be friends with you!

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.040
Right.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.290
Thanks.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:02.630
H-Hey, why are <i>you </i>crying, Yamada?

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:06.920
I'm just so relieved!

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.220
I can't help it!

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.340
You guys all okay?

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:12.350
July arrived.

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:16.640
We changed into our summer uniforms
and grew closer to one another.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:20.190
More and more often we called each other
by first names or nicknames.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:25.400
My personal goal:
call Sarasa Watanabe "Sarasa."

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:29.110
Unfortunately, it was
a tough challenge for me.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:33.030
Watanabe-<i>san</i>.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.740
What's up, Ai-<i>chan</i>?

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:37.370
I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.960
Okay! Don't fall in!

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:46.170
That's weird. I thought girls always
went to the bathroom together.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:48.720
Oh, right, Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:49.630
You wanna come with?!

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:50.590
No.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.930
Our midterm results
just got posted in the hall!

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:56.560
Wanna go check them out together?

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.060
Yeah.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.190
Sawa's top of the class, as usual.

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:03.190
"Midterm Test Results"
"#1: Sawa Sugimoto"

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:05.900
She did well enough before
to be our class rep, after all.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.270
Kaoru Hoshino

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:11.360
24th in the class. Not good, not bad.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.410
Yay! I moved up a bit!

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:17.950
I went from 40th to 39th!

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:18.870
Sa...

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:22.370
Nice, Watanabe-<i>san</i>.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:23.670
I know! I'm so happy, Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:25.040
I know! I'm so happy, Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:28.420
"#39: Sarasa Watanabe"
"#40: Ayako Yamada"

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.630
Oh, no...

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:32.180
I have the worst grades in the class now.

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:39.810
♬ Lead along by
the lovely spring breeze... ♬

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:44.350
Oh, come on! Yamada-<i>san</i>,
I can't hear you at all!

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.020
I'm sorry.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:51.900
Are you feeling okay, honey?
Getting enough sleep, eating well?

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.950
Yeah, I'm eating enough.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:56.450
First they told me not to eat,
now they want me to eat?

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.870
Can they make up their minds?

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:03.040
Take Me to Them

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:03.460
How did I even get in here, anyway?

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:06.750
I was eight when I saw my first
Kouka Troupe performance,

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:12.260
and I was completely captivated
by the fantastic world I saw.

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:19.010
Every year after that, I would always see
a Kouka show on my birthday,

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:22.940
and I would only sing
Kouka songs at karaoke.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:26.520
In middle school, I started taking ballet.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.610
My family runs a bakery.

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:30.780
We didn't have lots of money,

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:32.780
but when my parents saw
their quiet, shy daughter

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:35.030
passionately pursuing something,

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:38.700
they pushed themselves
the extra mile for me.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.540
I-I did it!

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.910
My adult sister thought...

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:46.210
What?! You wanna go into Kouka?!

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:50.170
Yeah. They have a music school in Kobe.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.670
I thought about applying.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:56.180
But you're only in tenth grade.
You can already apply?

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:57.760
Oh, yeah.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:04.350
Whoa, last year's admittance rate was
worse than Tokyo U? What the hell?!

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:08.610
Yeah, so I probably won't get in.
I just thought it'd be nice.

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:11.730
Why not try to get in, then?

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:14.280
Yeah, I know... wait, what?

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:18.450
You've always loved singing, Ayako.

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:22.490
There was never anything I wanted to do,
so I just snagged an office job.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:25.870
But if you've got a dream,
you should go after it, y'know?

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:30.290
And if you're wrong and totally get in,
I'll help pay for your tuition!

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:36.510
When I got accepted, my mom and dad
were so happy for me.

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:39.260
My sister, on the other hand, sobbed.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.560
You did it, Ayako!

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:46.980
You're freakin' amazing!
I'm so happy for you!

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:50.860
I have no right to say
I want to quit after all that.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:57.240
Or that I can't keep up with my classes.

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:15.050
I wanna play Sukeroku and stamp my feet
and walk out on the <i>hanamichi</i>!

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:17.930
Sounds great. I can't wait to see it.

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:23.220
Sara--

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.390
Watanabe-<i>san</i>, is everything okay?

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:27.430
Huh?

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:33.690
Oh, I'm okay! I just don't like
the sound of cicadas is all.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.940
And 'cause I'm tall,
I'm closer to the sun,

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:39.570
which means I get hit with more UV rays.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:40.910
Is that a thing?

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:45.080
Hey, guys, our family in Hokkaido
sent us some <i>monaka</i>!

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:47.160
Tokachi's known for their
super-good red beans!

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.830
Hokkaido Red Bean Monaka

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:53.000
I heard that in the past, if your
final first-year grades were bad,

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.340
they made you drop out.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:58.010
Guess that's how they
weeded out poor candidates.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:12:59.840
That's so mean!

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.680
Oh hey, Ai-<i>chan</i>, what was your rank?

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:06.520
24th. I'm gonna do better, though.

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:11.020
I finally know what I want to do,
so I'm gonna give it my all.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:13.400
Might as well aim for the top.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:19.240
Right, you just "haven't been
actually trying this whole time."

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:23.200
One day, I'm gonna be one of
the Kouka Troupe's top stars.

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:27.540
Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:30.040
I shouldn't. I shouldn't
compare myself to her.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:33.920
Naracchi's on a whole
different level than I am.

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:39.050
I can't seem to throw up anymore.

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:41.430
And fatties can't stay in Kouka.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:44.140
Oh, sis...

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:49.430
Hit that falsetto! Keep that
throat open and hold it!

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:53.900
Hold it! Keep going!

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:59.990
Yamada-<i>san</i>, what's the matter?
Are you sure you're feeling okay?

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:02.610
Sorry, sir. I'm fine.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.950
Yeah, sure, you're <i>sorry</i>.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.040
Hey, Yamada!

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:10.370
Did you lose weight?

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:13.000
Yes, I lost around five kilograms.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:15.460
Good. Don't hurt yourself, though.

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:18.800
I want you to give me a daily report on
everything you've eaten, starting today.

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.300
Yes, ma'am.

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:23.840
Do I have to lose even <i>more </i>weight?

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:25.920
Ayako Yamada Food Log

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.470
Why the long face, Tachibana-<i>sensei</i>?

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:33.100
It's Ayako Yamada.
She's binging and purging.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:37.480
That explains why she lost weight,
and why her fingers were so red.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:41.360
Tachibana-<i>sensei</i>, did you <i>really</i>
tell Yamada-<i>san </i>she was a "fatty"?

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:42.280
I sure did.

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:45.910
I can't believe you! Why were you
so cruel to her?!

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.870
You need to watch
what you say to these girls!

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:51.910
Onodera-<i>sensei</i>, while being
nice to them is all fine and dandy,

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:54.420
when they join the troupe,

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:57.750
they're going to be subjected
to all sorts of verbal abuse.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:01.510
And the more popular they become,
the more abuse they'll get.

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:02.920
S-Sure, but--

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:06.090
Weak women can't survive in show business.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:12.810
Or are you telling Yamada to be so
unremarkable that no one will hate on her?

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:15.140
Th-That's not what I'm--

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.310
She needs to grow a backbone now.

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:20.360
Sure, but Yamada-<i>san</i>
is especially sensitive.

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:23.610
Then if she quits, it's just proof
she'd never make it.

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:25.450
I'm sorry, but it's true.

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:28.950
In either case, we need to
get her to stop throwing up.

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:36.330
I bet your back hurts right here.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:40.170
Narata-<i>san</i>, what are you doing here?

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:42.420
I had to pee.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.470
Your back doesn't hurt from working out.

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:48.720
A girl in JPX was doing the same thing.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:52.720
Your stomach acid agitates
your esophagus. That's why it hurts.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:56.190
Your esophagus goes right up
the middle of your back.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:58.060
Yeah, so?!

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:00.770
Losing weight that way
won't make you prettier.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.110
I don't wanna hear that,

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:08.700
not from someone who's <i>always </i>been pretty!

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:12.160
I'm sorry.

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:26.340
I want my big sister...

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:30.760
"Class A Music Materials"

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:33.560
Today, we're going to use all our class
time to hear a solo from everyone!

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:37.230
It's fun to mix things up, right?

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:42.310
Pick a song you like out of these three.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:44.980
Why don't you start us off, Yamada-<i>san</i>?

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:49.860
Take Me to Them

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:50.450
Which song are you singing?

00:16:57.250 --> 00:16:59.620
Yamada-<i>san</i>? Are you okay?

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:05.420
Whoa, Aya!

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:07.090
--Aya-<i>chan</i>!
--Yamada-<i>san</i>!

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.000
Medical Center

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:11.510
Looks like regular pharyngitis.

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:15.430
Your immune system's responding,
and you've got a fever.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:19.060
You should take it easy for a few days
and get plenty of rest.

00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:21.400
Um, I'm...

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:25.320
It's hard to talk, too, huh?
You should rest your voice, too.

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:28.280
I'm a Kouka student.

